Title: "Current Implementation Notes"
Id: "d29002a5-f9a7-4223-8033-32a2a718ce45"

Text: "This page records the most important current implementation boundaries and
migration facts. The focused Formulation, Structural, Headers, Type Checking,
Rendering, and CLI chapters contain the normative detail."
Id: "ce52d87b-92fd-4974-856d-57ff257440bd"

SectionTitle: "Current Definition Model"
Id: "31d9e831-cc23-42db-ade3-e8117b449d17"

Text: "The present roles are:

- `Declares:` defines reusable types and interfaces. It supports `extends:`,
  `specifies:`, and `satisfies:`.
- `Defines:` defines typed values and operations. It supports `abstractly:`,
  value-supplying `specifies:`, and `expresses:`.
- `Realizes:` implements all components left open by an abstract `Defines:`.
- `Refines:` defines adjective properties and uses `specifies:` for its base or
  inherited refinement fact.
- `States:` defines reusable propositions.
- `Example:` records an ordered mixture of checked clauses and quoted prose.

`Requires: definition:` refers to a top-level `Defines:` item. Spec-infix
headings are allowed only on `Declares:`. `Declares:`, `Defines:`, `Realizes:`,
and `States:` require `called:` or `written:` documentation; `Refines:` requires
`adjective:`."
Id: "c71c341b-eb8e-42b2-8385-3e42836061e6"

SectionTitle: "Current Formulation Spellings"
Id: "9daf84d0-fffb-45b3-916e-9c097a040118"

Text: "- The universal unstructured type is `\\anything`; `\\opaque` is
  unsupported and no longer has those builtin semantics.
- Specification literals use anonymous subject `_`, not `?`.
- The only build spelling is `\type@value`. Hard builds `@!` and hard type
  introductions `is!` were removed.
- `Enables: view:` replaces the old nested cast-relation syntax. Its required
  `as:` is `<symbol> := <expression> is <type>`.
- Specification capabilities use directed `:->` or equivalent `:<->:` arrows.
- Concrete direct components use `..` in source, such as `\naturals..N` and
  `\naturals..succ(n)`. A bound value continues to use one dot.
- A command may end in one `#using{...}` or `#given{...}` context suffix.
- Builtin clause commands start with two backslashes and separate arguments
  with semicolons. The local-binding form is `\\let`; `\\given` is unsupported.
  The theorem-like top-level `given:` section remains supported."
Id: "1f1abc1d-6fde-4eeb-9eff-42032773a1b6"

SectionTitle: "Bindings And Branches"
Id: "3ab5903f-3c3c-4bcb-adc3-0d4e01f87acb"

Text: "Within an inherited semantic scope, the same defined symbol cannot be
introduced twice. This rejects duplicate header parameters and `:=` targets,
`using:` declarations that redeclare heading/target symbols, nested quantifiers
or `let:` groups that shadow outer bindings, and colliding `view: as:` symbols.
Placeholders local to separate function forms may repeat; callable names may
not.

Clause binding positions use the refined declaration parser, so refined types
are accepted consistently. A structural `piecewise:` group accepts zero or more
`elseIf:`/`then:` pairs between its initial branch and optional `else:`. Each
conditional branch is checked with its own condition assumed."
Id: "e00c3a0f-de87-4c74-aeda-4cf097549a35"

SectionTitle: "Specification And Rendering Details"
Id: "1662db61-1f89-47f5-92cf-242ffb8853c6"

Text: "Top-level `:=` assignments are accepted in `specifies:`. In a concrete
`Defines:` or `Realizes:`, they supply component values; in `Declares:` they may
tie a component to an already-known value. Capability and type inference follow
the assignment.

Direct component expressions are valid as ordinary expressions and as
specification subjects or targets. The source keeps `..`; rendered mathematics
shows one dot.

`called:` and `written:` placeholders normalize source placeholder suffixes. If
a heading parameter is `n_`, both `n_?` and `n?` substitute it, and rendering
does not expose the source underscore. Conditional fragments and parenthesis
modifiers remain supported."
Id: "07cbd937-0867-4e24-8aa9-119cca58389c"

SectionTitle: "Collection And Checker Behavior"
Id: "49e7aedb-cd45-4903-afc7-af93b97298c4"

Text: "A collection has one `mlg.json` and a `content/` tree. Every directory `toc`
lists all direct `.mlg` files and subdirectories exactly once. `mlg check`
normally inserts a fresh UUID into a top-level item missing `Id:` before semantic
validation, so checking, viewing, and exporting may update source files.

`using:` introduces definition-local symbols. A requirement mentioning an
unbound `using:` symbol is not imposed at an ordinary call site; when the caller
supplies that symbol with `#using{...}`, the corresponding instantiated
requirement is checked.

The checker validates syntax, signatures, scope, tracked facts, requirements,
target completeness, capabilities, builds, views, and structural invariants. It
does not prove mathematical truth. One-element tuples remain unsupported,
refined command expressions are not general expressions, and subset syntax is
intentionally narrow. Prose fences tagged `mlg` are checked as source in their
containing scope; `mlg-fragment` fences are illustrative and skipped. `mlg check
--watch` and `mlg view --watch` re-run when collection inputs change."
Id: "27cc3feb-8cb4-46b6-907f-456c645dda68"

SectionTitle: "Removed Or Renamed Syntax"
Id: "f293823a-8ba8-405e-8920-c4781944e254"

Text: "These spellings do not belong in current source:

- `\\opaque` (use `\\anything`)
- `? is T` spec literals (use `_ is T`)
- `@!`, `is!`, `\\coercion`, and `\\encoding`
- the builtin command `\\given` (use `\\let`; theorem-like `given:` sections
  are unchanged)
- nested `Enables: relation:`/`to:`/`represents:` groups (use `view:`/`as:`)
- `Refines: extends:` (use `Refines: specifies:`)
- top-level or relationship `means:` fields (use `specifies:`)
- the pre-swap roles of `Defines:` and `Declares:`
- `Section:`, `Subsection:`, and `Subsubsection:` (use `SectionTitle:` and
  `SubsectionTitle:`)."
Id: "ab6191ea-a95e-46a1-96b6-ac7597f25483"
